  "platformTutorialPlatformSubtitle": "{platform} background optimization tutorial",
  "platformTutorialDetailTitle": "{platform} background running guide",
  "platformTutorialGuideTitle": "{platform} background optimization guide",
  "platformTutorialGuideIntro": "These steps can help optimize Stroom’s background experience on {platform} devices so tasks can continue running in the background.",
  "platformTutorialStepsHeading": "Optimization steps",
  "platformTutorialTipsHeading": "Tip",
  "platformTutorialTipsDescription": "After completing these settings, return to the “Background Optimization” page and check that the status has updated. If you still have problems, see another platform’s guide or report the issue on GitHub.",
  "platformTutorialAndroidStep1Title": "Turn off battery optimization",
  "platformTutorialAndroidStep1Description": "Open Settings → Apps → Stroom → Battery, then choose “Unrestricted” or “Don’t optimize.” You can also tap “Ignore battery optimization” on this app’s “Background Optimization” page to add Stroom to the system power-saving allowlist. Paths vary by device brand.",
  "platformTutorialAndroidStep2Title": "Allow background activity",
  "platformTutorialAndroidStep2Description": "Open Settings → Apps → Stroom and enable “Allow background activity” and “Allow auto-start.” Some phones also require allowing auto-start in Security Center or Phone Manager.",
  "platformTutorialAndroidStep3Title": "Lock the background process",
  "platformTutorialAndroidStep3Description": "In the recent-apps view, swipe down on the Stroom card or tap its lock icon to prevent the system from clearing the app.",
  "platformTutorialAndroidStep4Title": "Allow notifications (Android 13+)",
  "platformTutorialAndroidStep4Description": "Android 13 and later require notification permission. Without it, the foreground notification for the background service is hidden, though the service still runs. The app requests permission when you first tap “Start service,” or you can enable it in Settings → Apps → Stroom → Notifications.",
  "platformTutorialAndroidStep5Title": "Ignore battery optimization",
  "platformTutorialAndroidStep5Description": "When you enable “Task completion notifications” in Stroom, the app requests the related permission. You can also check that Stroom is set to “Don’t optimize” in Settings → Apps → Special app access → Battery optimization.",
  "platformTutorialAndroidStep6Title": "Auto-start and background management on Android devices",
  "platformTutorialAndroidStep6Description": "Device manufacturers often add their own background controls:\n• Xiaomi/Redmi (MIUI/HyperOS): Settings → Apps → Permissions → Autostart; allow Stroom. Then open Battery → App battery saver → Stroom → No restrictions.\n• Huawei/Honor (EMUI/HarmonyOS): Settings → Apps → App launch → Stroom → Manage manually; allow auto-launch, secondary launch, and background activity.\n• OPPO/OnePlus/realme (ColorOS): Settings → Battery → App battery management → Stroom; allow full background activity.\n• vivo/iQOO (OriginOS): iManager → App management → Autostart; allow Stroom.",
  "platformTutorialAndroidStep7Title": "Turn off lock-screen cleanup and power-saving modes",
  "platformTutorialAndroidStep7Description": "Open Settings → Battery and turn off “Power saving” or “Ultra power saving.” Also set “Clear memory after locking” to “Don’t clear.” Power-saving modes restrict background activity and may affect task completion.",
  "platformTutorialIosStep1Title": "Enable Background App Refresh",
  "platformTutorialIosStep1Description": "Open Settings → General → Background App Refresh, find Stroom, and turn it on. Choose “Wi-Fi & Cellular Data” for the best experience.",
  "platformTutorialIosStep2Title": "Allow notifications",
  "platformTutorialIosStep2Description": "Open Settings → Notifications → Stroom and turn on “Allow Notifications.” Enable both banners and Notification Center so you can see task updates promptly.",
  "platformTutorialIosStep3Title": "Turn off Low Power Mode",
  "platformTutorialIosStep3Description": "Open Settings → Battery and turn off “Low Power Mode.” The system restricts background activity while this mode is on.",
  "platformTutorialIosStep4Title": "Understand iOS background limits",
  "platformTutorialIosStep4Description": "Versions before iOS 26 do not allow apps to stay in the background like Android apps. The system gives apps brief execution time only at certain times, such as Background App Refresh, location updates, or audio playback, and may suspend long-running tasks. We recommend:\n• Keep Stroom in the foreground for long-running tasks.\n• Return to the app periodically to refresh its background time.\n• Turn on “Task completion notifications” for important tasks.",
  "platformTutorialIosStep5Title": "Background tips while tasks run",
  "platformTutorialIosStep5Description": "iOS 26 and later support persistent background tasks. Tasks usually continue if you switch apps or lock the screen, though the system may stop them when resources are scarce; progress appears on the Lock Screen.\n\nEarlier iOS versions do not support persistent background tasks. Return to the app every few minutes (5–10 minutes is a guideline; the system decides) to refresh background time and prevent suspension.\n\nOn every version, do not swipe Stroom away in the app switcher; doing so immediately stops all running tasks.",
  "platformTutorialIosStep6Title": "Keep the app in the foreground",
  "platformTutorialIosStep6Description": "On versions earlier than iOS 26, apps have limited background time. For long-running tasks, keep Stroom in the foreground or return to it periodically to extend that time.",
  "platformTutorialWindowsStep1Title": "Minimize when closing the window",
  "platformTutorialWindowsStep1Description": "By default, clicking the window’s close button minimizes Stroom to the system tray (near the clock) so it can keep running. Restore it from the tray icon or “Show main window” menu. Do not quit while tasks are running. To exit, use “Exit application completely” on the “Background Optimization” page or choose “Quit Stroom” from the tray menu.",
  "platformTutorialWindowsStep2Title": "Turn off Battery Saver",
  "platformTutorialWindowsStep2Description": "Open Settings → System → Power & sleep and turn off Battery Saver. Alternatively, configure it to turn on only when the battery falls below a chosen level.",
  "platformTutorialWindowsStep3Title": "Allow background apps",
  "platformTutorialWindowsStep3Description": "Open Settings → Privacy & security → Background apps, find Stroom, and make sure it is enabled. On Windows 11, go to Settings → Apps → Installed apps → Stroom → Advanced options → Background app permissions and choose “Always.”",
  "platformTutorialWindowsStep4Title": "Turn off sleep mode (optional)",
  "platformTutorialWindowsStep4Description": "To keep Stroom running for long periods, open Settings → System → Power and set “Sleep” to “Never” (when plugged in only).",
  "platformTutorialWindowsStep5Title": "Add Stroom to startup",
  "platformTutorialWindowsStep5Description": "Open Task Manager (Ctrl+Shift+Esc) → Startup, find Stroom, and right-click “Enable.” Or open Settings → Apps → Startup and turn on Stroom.",
  "platformTutorialMacosStep1Title": "Minimize when closing the window",
  "platformTutorialMacosStep1Description": "By default, closing the window keeps Stroom running in the menu bar (top-right of the screen). Click its menu bar icon or choose “Show main window” to restore it. Do not quit while tasks are running. To exit, use “Exit application completely” on the “Background Optimization” page or choose “Quit Stroom” from the menu bar menu.",
  "platformTutorialMacosStep2Title": "Allow notifications",
  "platformTutorialMacosStep2Description": "Open System Settings → Notifications → Stroom and turn on “Allow Notifications.” We recommend enabling both banners and Notification Center.",
  "platformTutorialMacosStep3Title": "Turn off Low Power Mode (MacBook)",
  "platformTutorialMacosStep3Description": "Open System Settings → Battery → Power Adapter and turn off “Low Power Mode.” This mode restricts background activity.",
  "platformTutorialMacosStep4Title": "Keep the app active",
  "platformTutorialMacosStep4Description": "macOS places few restrictions on background apps. For long-running tasks, leave the Stroom window open. Avoid force-quitting the app; closing the window is enough.",
  "platformTutorialMacosStep5Title": "Launch at login (optional)",
  "platformTutorialMacosStep5Description": "Open System Settings → General → Login Items and add Stroom so it starts automatically when your computer starts.",
  "platformTutorialLinuxStep1Title": "Minimize when closing the window",
  "platformTutorialLinuxStep1Description": "By default, closing the window hides Stroom in the system tray (requires a desktop environment with StatusNotifierItem support and libayatana-appindicator3-dev at build time). Restore it from the tray menu using “Show main window.” Do not quit while tasks are running. To exit, use “Exit application completely” on the “Background Optimization” page or choose “Quit Stroom” from the tray menu.",
  "platformTutorialLinuxStep2Title": "Desktop environment settings",
  "platformTutorialLinuxStep2Description": "Depending on your desktop environment (GNOME, KDE, XFCE, etc.), open System Settings → Apps, find Stroom, and make sure background activity is not restricted.",
  "platformTutorialLinuxStep3Title": "Use a systemd service (optional)",
  "platformTutorialLinuxStep3Description": "For long-running background work, create a systemd user service. Create a stroom.service file under ~/.config/systemd/user/ and set ExecStart to the Stroom executable.",
  "platformTutorialLinuxStep4Title": "Disable sleep",
  "platformTutorialLinuxStep4Description": "For a server or desktop that needs to run for a long time, set HandleLidSwitch=ignore in /etc/systemd/logind.conf to prevent sleep when the lid closes.",
  "platformTutorialLinuxStep5Title": "Enable autostart",
  "platformTutorialLinuxStep5Description": "In GNOME, use Tweaks → Startup Applications → Add Stroom. Or create a stroom.desktop file under ~/.config/autostart/.",
  "platformTutorialWebStep1Title": "Keep the tab open",
  "platformTutorialWebStep1Description": "Web browsers do not support background services. Keep the Stroom tab open while tasks run; closing the tab or refreshing the page immediately interrupts them.",
  "platformTutorialWebStep2Title": "Prevent the browser from suspending the tab",
  "platformTutorialWebStep2Description": "Browsers may freeze inactive background tabs to save resources. Keep the Stroom tab in the foreground while tasks run, or interact with the page periodically to keep it active.",
